course: dictionary
lesson: 11388
title: Abundantly: more than enough
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Abundantly means in large amounts, so much that there is more than enough. «Wild strawberries grew abundantly in the meadow.» The meadow was full of them, far more than anyone could pick.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The school garden gave abundantly this year, so every class had carrots to take home.» The clue is every class had some to take home. Ask: would the word plenty fit here? If it would, abundantly is close in meaning.
explain: The word has a second meaning, very or completely. «Her face made it abundantly clear that she was not happy.» Here abundantly does not mean in large amounts. It means very clear. You will often meet it in books, news reports and teachers' speeches.
fact: Abundantly is an adverb: it tells you how something happens or how much there is.
fact: «Abundantly» means in large amounts, more than enough.
fact: «Abundantly» can also mean very or completely, as in «abundantly clear».
fact: A good check is to swap in plenty or very and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Abundantly» is slightly formal, so it is more common in writing than in everyday talk.
exercise: «Wild strawberries grew abundantly in the meadow.» What does abundantly mean here? | Sadly | *In large amounts, more than enough | Only just | Very slowly
exercise: «The teacher made the rule abundantly clear.» What does abundantly mean here? | Hidden away | In small amounts | Quietly | *Very clearly, completely
exercise: «The rain fell abundantly all day.» Which word could replace abundantly? | Rarely | Carefully | Quietly | *Plentifully
test: «The river ran abundantly after the storm.» Which meaning fits best? | *More than enough, in large amounts | Only just | Fast asleep | A tiny drip, very small
test: «Mum's note was abundantly clear: tidy your room now.» What does abundantly show here? | In small amounts | Hardly | *Very, completely | Angrily
exam: Which sentence uses abundantly to mean very clear? | «The plums grew abundantly on the tree.» | «The puppy slept abundantly on the rug.» | *«The sign was abundantly clear: keep out.» | «She ate abundantly at the party.»
